From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Garcia Brisa <d.garciabrisa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:59:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] launcher: explain the minimum macOS instead of failing to
 start

With ELECTROBUN_MACOS_LAUNCHER_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET below the app's deployment
target, the launcher opens on older macOS releases but the runtime it starts
(Bun needs macOS 13) cannot load there, so the app exits without a word.

ELECTROBUN_MACOS_REQUIRED_VERSION (zig -Dmacos-required-version) makes the
launcher read kern.osproductversion and, below that version, show a native
alert naming the app and the version it needs, then exit with status 1.
Unset, the launcher behaves as before.
---
 package/build.ts                       |   4 +
 package/src/launcher/build.zig         |  19 +++++
 package/src/launcher/macos_minimum.zig | 111 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 package/src/launcher/main.zig          |   4 +
 4 files changed, 138 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 package/src/launcher/macos_minimum.zig

